\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {V}{\ignorespaces Digital-twin end-to-end retrieval (DT4DDS; primary evidence). Per scenario and policy: share of retrievals whose output file is byte-identical to the stored file (no retrieval returned a wrong file), mean reads per retrieval (thousands; cluster-bootstrap 95\% CI over syntheses), the 0.99-quantile q99 (the budget to reserve), and the paired relative difference in mean reads against round-robin with verified stopping on retrievals where both succeeded (95\% CI). Static plans read fixed proportions until decodable and must reserve their q99 on every retrieval, so their mean cost equals q99; their proportions use per-container efficiencies measured in hindsight on the same scenario.}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
